{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The increment is implemented on the existing Spring XD 1.x codebase (Gradle multi-module build, Git) and its supported Java/Spring baseline; no upgrade of the overall framework baseline is part of this increment.",
    "U1: The Teradata NPE with the generic JDBC path will be root-caused and fixed where feasible; in addition, first-class support for the Hortonworks Connector for Teradata (org.apache.sqoop.teradata.TeradataConnManager) will be provided via documented configuration/packaging of the Sqoop job module so that --connection-manager works out of the box. Verification is done against a Teradata Express instance.",
    "U2: The logging directory will be externalized into a configurable property (e.g., XD_LOGGING_DIR / xd.logging.dir) resolved by the startup scripts and logging configuration, with ${xd.home}/logs kept as the default for backward compatibility; the RPM packaging will override the default to /var/logs/spring-xd.",
    "U3/U5: A new 'spring-bus' project will be created as a standalone Maven-published library; message-bus and serialization codec code will be extracted from the Spring XD repository preserving API compatibility, and Spring XD will consume them as Maven dependencies instead of in-repo modules.",
    "U4: The input/output type conversion (MimeType-based conversion of payloads, e.g., Tuple/JSON/POJO) will be moved into a spring-cloud-dataflow module with a generalized API so that custom modules producing/consuming custom domain objects can reuse it; Spring XD is adapted to depend on it.",
    "U6/U7: An XD Admin SPI based on the Module Launcher abstraction will be defined; the 'singlenode' implementation launches module containers within a single local JVM for local pipelines, and the Diego implementation uses the Diego Receptor API (LRPs/tasks) to run module containers on CF Lattice/Diego.",
    "U8: Handled as a time-boxed research spike: prototype spring-cloud-stream modules self-registering with a service discovery mechanism (e.g., Eureka-style registry) and assess how the Spring XD runtime on CF could discover and orchestrate them; deliverable is a prototype plus a findings/recommendations document, not a production feature.",
    "Unit tests are written as part of each development activity; cross-cutting integration/system testing and documentation are separate WBS activities."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer (the estimator) performs all work; estimates are pure effort in workdays (1 workday = 8 hours), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "The existing Spring XD 1.x source tree, build infrastructure, and CI are available and operational; only minor CI/build changes for the new repositories are needed.",
    "A Teradata Express test instance (or equivalent) and the Hortonworks Connector for Teradata archive are available for U1 verification; no license procurement effort is included.",
    "A CF Lattice/Diego test environment is available for U7; effort for deploying and testing on it is included, but not the provisioning of the environment itself.",
    "U8 is investigation-only; no production code changes from U8 are included in this increment.",
    "Estimates include coding, unit testing, self-review, and rework to a 'done' state; they exclude holidays, meetings unrelated to the increment, and organizational overhead.",
    "No clarifying questions were asked; where the specification is silent (e.g., exact SPI signatures, property names), reasonable naming/design choices were made as listed in the technical decisions."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment analysis and solution design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the eight user stories, define the XD Admin SPI approach, extraction strategy for spring-bus/spring-cloud-dataflow, and configuration design for logging; produce a short design outline per story.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Repository, build and CI setup for new modules",
      "activity_description": "Set up the new spring-bus project skeleton and any build/CI wiring required to publish Maven artifacts consumed by Spring XD (also covers spring-cloud-dataflow module placement).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Reproduce and root-cause Teradata JDBC NPE",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the NPE with the Teradata JDBC driver in the Sqoop job module, diagnose the failure path, and identify the fix or required connection-manager handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement Teradata support in Sqoop job module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the fix for the generic JDBC path and/or integrate the Hortonworks Teradata connector (TeradataConnManager) so that import jobs with --connection-manager work out of the box, including packaging/config changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Verify Teradata import jobs end-to-end",
      "activity_description": "Configure a Teradata Express test instance, run the tdTest Sqoop import job scenarios from the story, and verify data lands correctly in the target directory.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Externalize logging directory configuration",
      "activity_description": "Replace the hard-coded ${xd.home}/logs location with a configurable property resolved in startup scripts and logging configuration, keeping the current default for backward compatibility.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U2 - RPM packaging default and install verification",
      "activity_description": "Update RPM packaging so logs go to /var/logs/spring-xd by default and verify tarball/RPM installations start and log correctly with overridden and default values.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Create spring-bus project structure",
      "activity_description": "Define the module layout, packages, and versioning scheme for the spring-bus library that will host the message-bus (and later the codec).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Extract message-bus code into spring-bus",
      "activity_description": "Move the message-bus implementation out of the Spring XD repository into spring-bus, preserving API compatibility, and adapt its build/tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Migrate Spring XD to spring-bus dependency",
      "activity_description": "Remove in-repo message-bus code from Spring XD, wire the Maven dependency on spring-bus, and run the existing XD regression test suite.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Move type conversion to spring-cloud-dataflow",
      "activity_description": "Extract the input/output type conversion from Spring XD into spring-cloud-dataflow with a generalized API and adapt Spring XD to consume it as a dependency.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Validate custom domain object module scenario",
      "activity_description": "Build a sample custom module that produces/consumes a custom domain object using the moved conversion support and verify stream processing end-to-end.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Extract serialization codec into spring-bus",
      "activity_description": "Move the serialization codec from Spring XD into spring-bus, integrate it with the message-bus module, and update Spring XD to use the Maven dependency.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Codec regression and round-trip verification",
      "activity_description": "Run codec regression tests (round-trip serialization of supported types) and verify streams still pass payloads correctly through the moved codec.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Design XD Admin SPI contract",
      "activity_description": "Define the Admin SPI interfaces based on the Module Launcher abstraction that both the singlenode and Diego implementations will realize.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Implement singlenode Admin SPI runtime",
      "activity_description": "Implement the single-JVM 'singlenode' implementation of the XD Admin SPI that launches and manages modules locally via the Module Launcher.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Test local data pipeline use cases",
      "activity_description": "Deploy and run representative stream/job pipelines on the singlenode runtime and verify lifecycle operations (deploy, undeploy, status) work correctly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Study Diego Receptor API and design implementation",
      "activity_description": "Investigate the Diego Receptor API (LRPs/tasks) and design how module containers will be launched and supervised on CF Lattice/Diego.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Implement Diego Receptor Admin SPI",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Diego-based Receptor implementation of the XD Admin SPI that launches module containers on Lattice/Diego via the Module Launcher.",
      "most_likely_effort": 9
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Deploy and test on CF Lattice/Diego",
      "activity_description": "Deploy the runtime to a Lattice/Diego environment, run data pipeline use cases, and verify module orchestration and lifecycle behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Spike: s-c-s module self-registration with service discovery",
      "activity_description": "Time-boxed investigation and prototype of spring-cloud-stream modules self-registering with a service discovery mechanism so the Spring XD runtime on CF could discover and orchestrate them; includes a findings/recommendations write-up.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "Increment-wide integration and system testing",
      "activity_description": "Run cross-story integration and system tests across the modified components (Sqoop module, logging config, spring-bus/codec/conversion extractions, both Admin SPI runtimes) and fix defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update reference and user documentation: Teradata connectivity for Sqoop jobs, the new logging directory property and RPM behavior, the new library dependencies, and singlenode/Diego runtime usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "Final build, release packaging and review",
      "activity_description": "Produce release-ready builds of all affected modules (including publishing spring-bus artifacts), perform final review, tagging, and packaging.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 90
  }
}
